This license covers the Tidy Nest mod for Minecraft: its source code, jars, textures, documentation,
screenshots and updater scripts (together, "the Mod").

Official home: https://github.com/afkbirdgames/tidy-nest

In short: play it, stream it, run it on any server and put it in modpacks, as long as you credit
the author and point people to the official home. The author makes and publishes the versions.
Changes go through the official repository, and nobody else publishes their own version.


1. YOU MAY, FREE OF CHARGE

  a) Download, install and play the Mod, in single player and on any server, public or private,
     including servers that charge for access or ranks.
  b) Show the Mod in videos, streams, screenshots, articles and reviews, and monetise that
     content. A link to the official home in the description is appreciated.
  c) Include the unmodified official jar in a modpack or server pack, on any platform, if the
     pack credits the Mod and links to its official home.
  d) Change the Mod for your own private use, such as tweaking a value for your own world or
     server. You may not share or publish the changed version (see section 2).
  e) Suggest changes and report bugs by opening issues on the official repository (see
     section 3).


2. YOU MAY NOT, WITHOUT THE AUTHOR'S WRITTEN PERMISSION

  a) Publish, upload or share a modified version of the Mod, or a fork, port, remake, add-on or
     "continued" version of it.
  b) Reuse the Mod's code, textures, models or other assets in another project, or decompile
     or reverse-engineer the Mod to do so.
  c) Re-upload the Mod on its own (not inside a modpack) to another website or platform, or
     present it as your own work.
  d) Sell the Mod itself, or put it behind a paywall. Charging for a server, or monetising
     videos and streams, is fine (section 1).
  e) Remove or change this license, the copyright notice or the author's credit.

Permission for anything in section 2 can be given by the author in writing, for free or under a
paid agreement, as the author chooses. Ask by opening an issue on the official repository.
Permission covers only what it explicitly says.


3. CONTRIBUTIONS

If you send an issue, idea, bug report or other contribution to the official repository, you
agree that the author may use, change and publish it as part of the Mod under this license, with
no payment owed. The author decides what is included and released.


